hared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"DvQ9LueDdw3u-eeROpcX0A","review_id":"d93QY_oRgg6AY8VcjOP2Ww","date":"2018-01-04T21:15:37","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9391379356384277,"text_excerpt":"Being in the medical field I just had to check this place out. For $5 and about an hour you can truly get an idea of how medicine and pharmacy was practiced in early America. Lots of great exhibits and a good guide map to interpret them. Nothing gross but probably above the kids' heads. I think it is a cool diversion to see the pieces in the old NOLA pharmacist's house but probably more geared to people with medical knowledge."},{"business_id":"DvQ9LueDdw3u-eeROpcX0A","review_id":"9OzwZxFiVDWRaEIudqYKrw","date":"2018-07-02T00:01:20","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9387118816375732,"text_excerpt":"The Pharmacy Museum was one of my favorite places to see in New Orleans! Not only was the museum itself already extremely interesting and different, but we also had an amazing tour guide (Owen) who was really enthusiastic, knowledgeable, and funny. The tour alone lasted about one hour and was very inexpensive for the amount of rich information that was delivered (and in such a fascinating way). After the tour, which took place downstairs, we spent about 45 minutes exploring the rest of the museum, including the second floor. So much interesting content. So worth it!"},{"business_id":"DvQ9LueDdw3u-eeROpcX0A","review_id":"bQKmumGznTtdsMK5pN0IaQ","date":"2019-04-22T08:24:20","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9307904243469238,"text_excerpt":"A relatively small but super cool museum! My friend and I stumbled upon this place on Yelp and we were lucky enough to pass by around 1 PM which is when they have a guided tour for $5/person. The guide was quirky, informative, and funny! Such a unique place and would definitely recommend to any health care worker!"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
